pref-translate-help = Built-in services only need their API key: get a DeepSeek key from platform.deepseek.com, and a Tencent Hy-MT2-Pro key from the TokenHub console (console.cloud.tencent.com/tokenhub/apikey). The base URL and model show the built-in preset (read-only); each service's key is stored separately and loaded when switching. Switching the service fills in its recommended chunk size (DeepSeek 6000 / Hy-MT2-Pro 2500, still manually editable); chunking is paragraph-adaptive, only oversized paragraphs are split at whole-sentence boundaries, and code blocks and formulas are never sent to the API.
pref-translate-custom-help = The custom endpoint needs an OpenAI-compatible base URL (including /v1, e.g. https://api.openai.com/v1), an API key, and a model name; the base URL and model become editable. Only Markdown output is translated; HTML output is left as is.
